Z||000019||Motorhead||04-11-99||05:31 AM||||Got'ya Ogre.  I realized which "grates" you were talking about after I posted the response.<p>Still, that blank rear quarter panel on the right side of the car seems like wasted space.<p>Since I'm moving the battery to the front compartment anyway, I figure that gained space in the engine compartment could be used to introduce fresh air via a duct from that blank rear quarter panel on the right side.<p>I thought about the old Indy style snorkel, but ruled it out as impractical for ease of access to the engine, not to mention the fact that rear viewing in this car is bad enough allready, without adding another obstacle to have to look around for oncoming traffic.<p>Unfortunately I exchanged the cracked head for the new one, core charge! Yes the new head is a remanufacture, but sure is pretty sitting up there on the block.<p>Porting! I've never done a port and polish job before, but I've got an old Mopar buddy helping me through this procedure, the guy is a real artist. We're gonna' balance and port my Z-car turbo motor when we're done with the Fiero.<p>I've got to thank Cliff,[got the name right this time] for this forum, saved me alot of running around sourcing parts.<p>Sorry for being so long winded!<p><br>
